+## Usage reported to afterModelResponse
+
+`afterModelResponse` is called once per user message, after the round loop exits, and reports what the turn cost at the provider, not what its final call cost (re-cinq/HALEngine#93). Its third argument is the turn's usage summed across every provider call the turn made, and its fourth is the per-call breakdown — one `UsageMetadata` per round that reported usage, in round order — so a consumer that wants provider-call granularity keeps it. A round whose provider reported no usage contributes nothing rather than a zero, so a partial reporter cannot turn the total into `undefined` or `NaN`, and a turn where no round reported usage still reports no total. A turn that ran no tools made exactly one provider call, so its sum is that call's usage, and the hook receives what it has always received on that path.
+
+- A turn driven through two tool rounds reports the sum of both provider calls' usage, with the per-round breakdown beside it ([validated by: reports usage covering every provider call of a two-tool-round turn](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L64)).
+- Rounds whose provider reported no usage are left out of the sum without making it `undefined` or `NaN`, and a turn where no round reported still reports no total, with an empty breakdown ([validated by: counts only the rounds that reported usage, and reports no total when none did](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L94)).
+- A turn with no tool calls reports exactly what it reported before this change — the single provider call's usage ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+
